📖 What I Learned
Used ps to view running processes.
Used top to monitor CPU and memory usage in real time.
Checked disk usage using df and df -h.
Viewed RAM and swap memory using free and free -h.
Used vmstat to monitor system performance.
Learned how nohup keeps a command running after the terminal is closed.
Viewed command output stored in nohup.out using cat, head, and tail.
Explored kill and fuser commands for process management.
🚀 Key Takeaways
Linux provides powerful tools to monitor system performance.
Process management is an essential DevOps skill.
Understanding CPU, memory, disk, and background jobs helps in troubleshooting servers.
